# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leaderboard configuration
#
# The global board runs on PlayFab title 1095E4 by default (hard-coded in
# src/engine/Leaderboard.ts). The Title ID is PUBLIC — it ships in every
# client; there is NO secret key and NO backend of our own.
#
# Override it here (another title), or set it to "local" for a device-only
# board (localStorage, no network at all).
#
# PlayFab title setup (Game Manager, already done for 1095E4):
#   • Settings → API Features:
#       – "Allow client to post player statistics"            ON
#       – "Disable player creation using Client/LoginWithCustomId" OFF
#         (the game's invisible device login uses that call)
#   • Progression → Statistics: "HighScore", entity title_player_account,
#     one column "Score", aggregation Max, reset Manual.
#   • Community → Leaderboards: "HighScore", linked to the HighScore
#     statistic, column Score Descending, reset Manual.
#   (New titles can't use the legacy "Leaderboards (Legacy)" /
#    Client/UpdatePlayerStatistics APIs — they return ProductDisabledForTitle.)
#
# Free plan: Development mode allows 1,000 lifetime players per title. Past
# that the title must move to Pay-as-you-go (no monthly fee, a payment method,
# fractions of a cent per thousand calls). Until then new players just see
# their device board.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_PLAYFAB_TITLE_ID=
